<!--
  Words the TCP transcription misread or left out, corrected as the source is read
  (colophon/sources.py); the TCP file itself is untouched. No scan of the 1673 printing is to be
  had: each is a keying slip (not a word, or nonsense where it stands) that the 1676 printing,
  set from 1673, reads as the sense requires (archive.org scan, work/surest-way/scan-1676; read
  with Kraken and Tesseract, collated, and checked by sense). Variants of the 1676 printing are
  not taken. Made by work/surest-way/slips/assemble.py; edit there.

  fix/@pb: the printed page. before + tcp + after: the transcription's text there (in one text
  node; any white space matches any white space), found exactly once on that page. print: what
  is printed in place of tcp (empty tcp: words the transcription left out). evidence: kept in a
  comment in the TEI.
-->
